title:: BMSpeakerListVisualiser
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - visualise the positions of a speaker list in a window
categories:: Classes

Description::

BMSpeakerListVisualiser provides a 3D visualisation of the positions of a speaker list (a link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMInOutArray::) in a space. You can rotate the visualisation trackball style with the mouse, and zoom vertically using the slider at the top.

Speakers will be labelled on the back with their names, and colour coded according to subarray membership (using first subarray found).

This class can also be used in conjunction with link::Classes/Other/Swarm Granulation/BMSwarmGranulator:: and link::Classes/Other/Swarm Granulation/BMBoidSpace:: to visualise grain boid positions.

See also: link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractGUI::, link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMSpeaker::, link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMInOutArray::, link::Classes/Other/Swarm Granulation/BMSwarmGranulator::, link::Classes/Other/Swarm Granulation/BMBoidSpace::

CREATEMETHODS::

method:: new	
Create a new BMSpeakerListVisualiser.

argument:: speakerList
An instance of link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMInOutArray::.


INSTANCEMETHODS::
				
method:: showBoids
Turn grain boid drawing on or off.

argument:: bool
A link::Classes/Boolean:: value.


method:: boidPositions
Set the positions at which to draw the grain boids. The x-axis is specified within the range of +/- 1. The y and z axes are sized proportionally. Normally these are derived using BMBoidSpace's positions method.

argument:: boidsArray
An Array of Arrays in the form [[x1, y1, z1], [x2, y2, z2], ...]


Examples::

code::
////// 5.1 Array (-0.1)
(
// make a speaker list
l = [[-30, 'L'], [30, 'R'], [0, 'C'], [-110, 'Ls'], [110, 'Rs']].collectAs({|el, i|
	BMSpeaker.newFromSpherical(el[1], i, el[0], 0, 2);
}, BMInOutArray);
)
v = BMSpeakerListVisualiser(l); // let's look at it


////// American style 8 Channel Ring
(
l = [[0, 'F' ], [45, 'FR'], [90, 'R'], [135, 'BR'], [180, 'B'], [-135, 'BL'], [-90, 'L'], [-45, 'FL']].collectAs({|el, i|
	BMSpeaker.newFromSpherical(el[1], i, el[0], 0, 2);
}, BMInOutArray);
)
BMSpeakerListVisualiser(l); // let's look at it


////// zig zag partial dome
(
l = [[-22.5, 40, 'Upper1'], [22.5, 40, 'Upper2'], [-67.5, 40, 'Upper3'], [67.5, 40, 'Upper4'], [-112.5, 40, 'Upper5'], [112.5, 40, 'Upper6'], [-157.5, 40, 'Upper7'], [157.5, 40, 'Upper8'], [-45, 0, 'Lower1'], [45, 0, 'Lower2'], [-90, 0, 'Lower3'], [90, 0, 'Lower4'], [-135, 0, 'Lower5'], [135, 0, 'Lower6'], [0, 0, 'Lower7'], [180, 0, 'Lower8']].collectAs({|el, i|
	BMSpeaker.newFromSpherical(el[2], i, el[0], el[1], 2);
}, BMInOutArray);
l.defineSubArray(\upper, l.keys[(0..7)]);
l.defineSubArray(\lower, l.keys[(8..15)]);
)
BMSpeakerListVisualiser(l); // note subArray colour coding

////// Big BEAST Array
BMSpeakerListVisualiser(Object.readArchive("BigSpeakerArray".resolveRelative));
::
